        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ताल",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ताल — tāl — \"rhythm; a beat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ढोलाचा ताल ऐकून सगळे नाचू लागले. ḍholācā tāl aikūn sagḷe nācū lāgle. Hearing the drum's rhythm, everyone began to dance."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ताल (tāl) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit tāla, \"clapping the hands, musical time\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
